    "Adam Mickiewicz University, Poznań, Poland\nJavaScript is disabled\nIn order to ensure full functionality of the current page, scripting needs to be enabled.\nScripting can be enabled in your browser's settings.\ntutaj\nErasmus+ and Exchange programme students\ninaugurated the new academic year\ndiscover more\nTHE World University Rankings 2027\nAdam Mickiewicz University, Poznań is one of the highest-ranked universities in Poland\nRead more\n32nd General Assembly of CGU\nOn September 13–15, the Compostela Group of Universities Assembly continues at AMU\nFind out more\nAMU ranks highly in global Japanese studies\nThe 18th EAJS International Conference came to an end on Sunday 30 August\nDiscover more\nErasmus+ and exchange programme students\ninaugurated the new academic year\nTHE World University Rankings 2027\nAMU is one of the highest-ranked universities in P\n32nd General Assembly of CGU\nOn September 13–15, the Compostela Group of Univ\nAMU ranks highly in global Japanese studies\nThe 18th EAJS International Conference came to an\n,\nWelcome to AMU\nAdam Mickiewicz University is the major academic institution in Poznań and one of the top Polish universities. Its reputation is founded on tradition, the outstanding achievements of the faculty and the attractive curriculum.  The mission of the University is to advance knowledge through high quality research and teaching in partnership with business, professions, public services and other research and learning providers.\nResearchers have investigated the interstellar comet 3I/ATLAS\n07 october 2026\nThe raw material challenges of the energy transition\n07 october 2026\nFree legal consultations for international students in Poland – Academia Law Hub project\n07 october 2026\nThree universities, one degree programme. The EPICUR Triple Master has kicked off!\n06 october 2026\nStaff from the AMU Faculty of Pedagogy and the Fine Arts at the 12th Euro-Asian Mediations Biennale - DIGITAL SPECIES in Guangzhou\n06 october 2026\nRead More\n13 october 2026\nLecture by Prof. Laura Moss (University of British Columbia)\n16 october 2026\nInternational academic conference: ‘Literature, Language and Cultural Heritage of the Sinti and Roma in School and Higher Education in Poland and Germany: A Comparative Perspective’\n22 october 2026\nISQI Seminar – Prof. Marcin Markiewicz\n5 november 2026\nPolar Day 2026\nRead More\nThe University\nIt is a centre of academic excellence where research and teaching are mutually sustaining, and where the context within which research is conducted and knowledge is sought and applied is international as much as regional and national.   The University continuously extends and updates research programs and contents of study curricula, with a special emphasis on their interdisciplinary and international nature. 613 projects are currently being carried out by international and national research teams.\n613\nresearch projects\nAdam Mickiewicz University, Poznań - NAWA WelPack AMU\nAMU Welcome Message\nAMU Online Admission System\nNAWA WelPack AMU - Humanities\nAMU Virtual Tour\nStudy at AMU\nThe University is organized into 20 Faculties where mostly training-through-research is offered together with high quality supervision according to the HRS4R policy adopted at AMU. Each fellow may take advantage of the supervisor’s experience or contacts. AMU has received the \"HR Excellence in Research\" award and has implemented the principles of the European Charter for Researchers and the Code of Conduct for the Recruitment of Researchers.\nStudy Programs\nApply NOW\nErasmus +\nShort time bilateral exchange"
  ],
